goodbye.md

Goodbye is one of the oldest rituals of human connection — a small ceremony we perform at the edge of every parting. It began as "God be with you," a blessing wrapped in a word, offered to travelers setting out into an uncertain world. We say it because leaving, even briefly, carries a quiet weight. It acknowledges that the time shared mattered, that the other person matters, and that the world between two people shifts the moment they walk in different directions. In saying goodbye, we mark the moment honestly, refusing to let it slip away unnoticed.